module test.claim.roadmap.roadmap_operator_close_retire_witness

// EXECUTING WITNESS for the operator CLOSE / RETIRE routes (operator ruling 2026-11-04).
//
// What these claims prove by RUNNING, not reading:
//   CLOSE   — a merged-PR close succeeds and the acceptance is DURABLE (a fresh read of the same
//             bytes sees the live receipt) and immediately visible; the same inputs give the same
//             durable record; an UNMERGED PR refuses carrying its state; a PR absent from the roster
//             is not merged; a GitHub roster that cannot be READ refuses FAIL-CLOSED with nothing
//             written (manager condition three); missing receipt evidence names its field; the
//             receipt's own facts are the idempotency identity — a replay answers the FIRST
//             recording, and other content for a closed node refuses; a log that cannot be READ
//             refuses the close rather than being written onto blind.
//   ONE HOME — acceptances live ONLY in the roadmap event log: the load replays ONE chain, and two
//             acceptances of one node are REFUSED at load, located — no silent double-count, no
//             silent drop (manager condition one). The fabric acceptance partition and the committed
//             seed jsonl are gone, and these claims assert the close never touches the former.
//   DEPENDENTS — a child blocked on an unaccepted node becomes ready once the parent's acceptance
//             is live.
//   RETIRE  — the standing fold reads retired from ANY prior standing (the unsettled-review world),
//             later events never move it; a terminal lineage owes NOTHING at the belt's one
//             obligation question; a closed node's lineage reads terminal to the belt read (the one
//             rule), and an unreadable history fails closed rather than guessing open.
//   ROUTES  — the serve routes refuse anonymously, refuse without the CSRF token, name an unknown
//             node, refuse a malformed retire form, and the close route fails closed when GitHub
//             cannot be read.
//
// Everything wet lives under the run's temp dirs; the only durable effect is an event append
// through the modeled route (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_issue_command issue_command_apply).

